From Damian.Lidgard at Dal.Ca  Thu Nov 26 13:39:14 2020
From: Damian.Lidgard at Dal.Ca (Damian Lidgard)
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2020 12:39:14 +0000
Subject: [tlocoh-info] Response to : Sampling frequency graph (Cassandra
	Arkinstall)
In-Reply-To: <mailman.1.1606388409.3065.tlocoh-info@lists.r-forge.r-project.org>
References: <mailman.1.1606388409.3065.tlocoh-info@lists.r-forge.r-project.org>
Message-ID: <60412576-42DC-4F04-92C8-5534B243F8A5@dal.ca>

I think this is less about T-LoCoH and perhaps more about how to approach the analysis. T-LoCoH’s strength is in using frequent data points to examine fine-scale temporal and spatial site use. I might be worthwhile to consider using a broad analysis for the two months based on 1 to 2 fixes per day (randomly choosing 1 to 2 data points in the second month) and the a finer scale analysis based on the second month of data (assuming you only have two months of data).

This suggestion of course is given without knowing what your questions are.

Damian

